WEBVTT

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.910
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold
in Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.980
Kingdom of Ambitions

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:39.430
You see, I left my country with some of 
my friends, and came to this one by boat.

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.950
But I got separated from them.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:45.910
After wandering for several days, 
I met you, Colette.

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:48.180
That must have been rough...

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.380
And yet you protected me from 
those wolves, and even got hurt...

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:56.120
Thanks, Mitsuha!

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.810
Agh!

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.390
Don't do that! Seriously!

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.560
It's gonna crack!

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:04.110
Uncle! I said uncle!

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.610
Good morning, Tobias.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.060
Morning, Mitsuha.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:16.110
<i>Matches and lighters really 
are magical items.</i>

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.370
I can't stand the smell of these toilets!

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.220
I want an air freshener!

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.550
Hey there, wolf-slaying hero.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.860
Are your wounds healed up?

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.240
Well, I suppose.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.300
I heard she crossed the sea to get here.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.900
Huh, from so far away?

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.930
Never thought someone from a foreign 
country would visit this place.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.410
<i>Now's my chance to gather some information!</i>

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.890
This sure is a nice place.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.690
What's it like to live here?

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.530
Lord Bozes, who rules over 
this land, is a reasonable man.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.880
So Bozes is the name of this country's king?

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.690
He's not the king, he's our lord.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:06.280
Count Claus von Bozes.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.530
A count...

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:11.540
<i>So "von" must be a title 
indicating nobility.</i>

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:15.930
When we have poor wheat or vegetable 
harvests, he'll reduce the yearly levies.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:16.950
I see...

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.690
He widened the roads into town, as well.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:23.230
That's right, to make it easier 
to haul crops and game.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.420
Oh!

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.510
<i>He sounds like a pretty nice person.</i>

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:29.660
And he's a powerful man 
with influence in the government.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:30.730
Oh, my!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.280
<i>He sounds like a good way to start 
making my way up in this world.</i>

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.540
You want to go to the royal capital?

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.620
That's quite a distance from here.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:39.740
But...

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.480
I promised the friends I was separated from

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.530
that we'd meet back up in the capital 
if anything happened.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.240
What? Mitsuha...

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.620
There's a passenger wagon setting off 
for town tomorrow morning.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:54.580
Going from the lord's town to the capital 
will take seven days by wagon.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.250
A child traveling on her own 
that far away...

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.210
I'm an adult.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.720
Wh-What'd you say?!

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:04.640
Come on...

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.680
No way...

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.110
I'm an adult.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:12.870
If you're an adult, 
that'd make us old geezers!

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:13.810
Right?

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:18.510
In my country, I'm considered an adult!

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.180
O-Oh...

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:24.980
Is that right?

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.200
It's a big world out there, huh?

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.020
So what time does the wagon set off?

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.640
Huh? I said in the morning.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.750
I'm asking what time in the morning...

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.370
Morning is morning!

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.440
I see...

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:38.670
<i>How vague...</i>

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:39.670
No!

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.880
Colette?

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.900
No, no, no!

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:49.140
You can't leave, Mitsuha!

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.430
Don't throw a fit.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:53.480
Well...

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.930
You mustn't give Mitsuha a hard time.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.360
I'm sad about it, too.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.280
The two of us made it out 
of that tough spot together.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:09.030
Mitsuha...

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.600
You saved my life, Colette.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.280
I'm truly grateful.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:22.470
But I'm sorry. 
There's a reason I need to go.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:26.050
My friends that I'm looking for 
should be heading to the capital.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.370
But...

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.670
Then, I promise...

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:31.180
One day, I'll make sure I come back.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.770
But, but...

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:37.690
You're smart, so you must realize 
already that you can't stop me.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:42.360
So I want you to send me off with a smile.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:48.580
Every time I think of you 
until we meet again,

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.340
I don't want your crying face 
to be what comes to mind.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.390
I like it better when you smile, Colette.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:05.240
I said don't do that!

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:17.940
Here you go.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:40.120
It looks like the ranks of nobility 
are the same as on Earth.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.750
Coincidences are, at times, inevitable.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:44.460
Here.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:54.430
<b>About Ranks of Nobility
Duke
 Marquess
No2 Count
 Viscount
 Baron</b>

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:48.060
The ranks go duke, marquess, 
count, viscount, and baron,

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.350
so if you exclude dukes 
who are tied to royalty,

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:54.430
Count Bozes is second from the top, 
a prime piece of real estate.

