I'm here, Captain.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.330
How cheerful, considering your requests...

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.330
So were you able to appraise the gold coin?

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:40.520
Yeah.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:43.550
At this karat, it's worth 
around $200 right now.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:46.360
<i>Which means...</i>

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:49.510
<i>Around 80,000 gold for 2,000,000,000 yen!</i>

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:53.560
So would it be possible to pay 
using these coins in the future?

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:57.300
Yeah. I see no reason 
to turn down real gold.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:05.260
Ultimately, I'm hoping to cash in 
some tens of thousands of these coins.

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:07.570
That depends on the handling fee.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:11.070
Of course I'll sweeten the deal for you.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:15.540
Sounds good. You've got a deal.

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:19.000
Then, we'll discuss it at a later date.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:22.000
Okay, then, let's move on to the gun lecture!

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:27.300
When handling guns, there are some 
rules you must abide by at all times.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:30.260
Those who do not are unfit to possess a gun.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.470
Yes!

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.650
First, treat all firearms 
as though they're loaded,

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:44.190
and always aim them in a safe direction.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:52.200
Second, never aim a firearm 
at anyone other than your target.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:57.430
Third, keep your finger off the trigger 
until the moment you aim for a target,

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:59.630
and keep it outside the trigger guard.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.350
Fourth...

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:08.510
Always be aware of where your target is 
and what lies beyond it.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.040
You should never have stray bullets.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.400
Is that understood?

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:13.220
Yes.

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:15.930
Come with me.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.840
All right, let's begin.

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:29.380
First, a subcompact pistol, the Walther PPS.

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:32.730
9mm caliber, 549g.

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:35.910
Eight rounds per magazine, 
and one round in the chamber.

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:38.380
Whoa!

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:46.120
Should be more than enough for self-defense.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:48.440
Okay, let's have you fire some rounds.

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:49.420
Right!

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:54.140
Grip it with your left hand 
wrapping around your right hand.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.090
Like this?

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:58.470
That's right. Don't touch the slide.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.100
I missed.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:09.200
Well, that's how it goes at first.

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:17.010
